    {
      "id": "claim_7fe290c26e3040d497b48278fd265c62",
      "statement": "The report groups items by what actually goes wrong, because the fix differs. `unusable` holds every mode not in `_PROXY_MODES_OK` (`proxied`, `passthrough`) and not `omit` — including `placeholder` and any mode this version has never heard of, since an unknown mode is not assumed safe — and names the per-item fixes (`@proxy(domain=...)` on the item, `@proxy=passthrough`, or `@sensitive=false`). `withheld` holds the `omit` items as resolver failures, not routing mistakes, and is printed even though `_varlock_resolve` also fails on the schema because it names the ITEM where that error names the DIRECTORY. `passthrough` items get a dim note, not a warning, because they are a declared decision preserving the full pre-proxy exposure. Proxied items are not reported at all.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/harnessed/launchenv.py#L381-L427",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:530c2fbacbeb7246151c925f7a6e1093f08a734aacd8bd1330b8354f113ea984:"
