    {
      "id": "claim_1ec402d4715443ee9fba0718de908c0e",
      "statement": "#388 is half-landed per the roadmap's 2026-09-09 snapshot: Phase 1 shipped the broker lifecycle, the loopback door and `--no-secrets` — a container launch whose composed schema opts in starts a real host-side broker (broker.py, Topology B, fail-fatal) wired to the pod via 169.254.1.1 — but the behaviour change did not ship, and the launcher still resolves real values into the container env at launch, so both halves are needed before the security property is real and only the first is in. The shipped `.env.schema.example` still carries no `@proxy` annotation, so a schema with no `@proxy` is every schema shipped today and every stack shipped today takes the no-broker path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.env.schema.example",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:95d86825bdc56fa19292860f7afa864207d835df9004c82fe2f4e9bee5bea845"
        },
        {
