    {
      "id": "claim_9b8e33783fd84caa92678bd44bf89f70",
      "statement": "`launchenv.proxy_schema_dirs(project_path)` is the gate on starting a secrets broker at all: it returns the schema dirs that opted into the proxy model in `--env-file` order (user-global `~/.config/harnessed` first, then the project), returns [] when `varlock` is not on PATH, and reuses `_schema_declares_proxy`, so it costs two file reads and no subprocess — a launch that opted into nothing must not buy a `varlock proxy rules` call that can sit on a 1Password unlock prompt, and the test pins that no varlock subprocess runs at all, not merely that no broker was recorded. It deliberately mirrors the dir selection of `_resolve_launch_secrets` so the broker resolves the SAME composed set the `--env-file` path resolves; a subset would hand the pod placeholders (#439) for items the broker never loaded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/harnessed/launchenv.py#L430-L452",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6bd139d38c620ea27f4ba45a94ff140457b63652df1286bd5e9a351f5b97031:"
