        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_597fa7000b974acd8e796c62b3fe0f8e",
      "statement": "`launcher._broker_start_for` starts a host secrets broker for the instance only when the composed schema carries a `@proxy` annotation and `--no-secrets` was not passed; the flag reaches the backend as the `NO_SECRETS` environment variable, the same mechanism as `--no-firewall`, with only `1`/`true`/`yes` (case- and whitespace-tolerant) counting as truthy. A failed start is FATAL (issue #437, SPEC decision 2): the launch exits 1 rather than leaving a pod wired half-way to a proxy that is not there, and the failure message is fixed and value-free by construction — it names the instance and the `--no-secrets` escape hatch and never echoes the exception, so no resolved value can reach the user through it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/harnessed/launcher.py#L1304-L1347",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dac42bc8a3f8c0a51f9ae82fb44152ea283a65240d3060f23c1a59aa108342dc:"
