    {
      "id": "claim_45ab2b42381844d6b7c1d3911ac617a5",
      "statement": "The parser-drift risk `_varlock_proxy_modes` itself names has materialized in the live layer: since 2026-08-28 the real-podman suite has failed every run with four tests, all in `TestVarlockProxyRulesOutput`, because `varlock proxy rules` output no longer parses (issue #462) — the roadmap's named reason the live layer is red. The hermetic tests feed canned text and cannot notice the move; the live class exists precisely because it does, and its assertion message is the refuse-to-guess contract speaking: `modes is None` means a header changed or the declared `Secrets (N)` count disagreed with the parsed lines.",
